WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.181
Development workflows need convenience without normalizing unsafe secret handling.

2
00:00:05.181 --> 00:00:10.742
Developers need to run the app locally, test database behavior, and debug configuration.

3
00:00:10.742 --> 00:00:20.220
The safe pattern is to support local productivity while keeping sensitive values out of source code, shared samples, and long-lived support artifacts.

4
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.483
ASP.

5
00:00:21.483 --> 00:00:24.516
NET Core Secret Manager is for development only.

6
00:00:24.516 --> 00:00:31.973
It helps keep local secrets out of project files, but it should not be treated as encrypted production secret storage.

7
00:00:31.973 --> 00:00:38.607
It is a developer convenience for local workflows, not a production vault or lifecycle management system.

8
00:00:38.607 --> 00:00:45.621
Environment variables can also keep local secrets out of source code, but local machines still need protection.

9
00:00:45.621 --> 00:00:53.330
Workstations can have terminal history, shell profiles, local logs, copied command output, screenshots, and support chats.

10
00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:58.511
Local values should be scoped to local or development resources whenever possible.

11
00:00:58.511 --> 00:01:04.766
Local database accounts should have limited privileges and should not reuse production credentials.

12
00:01:04.766 --> 00:01:10.137
A developer should not need production database access to run ordinary local tooling.

13
00:01:10.137 --> 00:01:17.214
When production access is necessary for a narrow operational task, it should follow a separate approved process.

14
00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:18.478
appsettings.

15
00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.742
Development.

16
00:01:19.742 --> 00:01:27.198
json should not contain shared sensitive values that could be committed, copied into examples, or reused across teams.

17
00:01:27.198 --> 00:01:36.739
If a file must show the shape of a connection setting, use placeholders and documentation that points developers to the correct local secret mechanism.

18
00:01:36.739 --> 00:01:38.003
.

19
00:01:38.003 --> 00:01:46.027
gitignore, sample files, onboarding docs, support runbooks, and local setup scripts should be reviewed as part of the workflow.

20
00:01:46.027 --> 00:01:54.305
Many secret exposures happen outside the main application code path, through the supporting material that helps people run the app.
